{"resourceIdentifier":"5172","resourceName":"Project Akwaaba | Forest Ecosystem Restoration in Ghana","description":"Rainforest Builder Ltd is an integrated tropical forest restoration company founded in 2022 to pioneer tropical forest ecosystem restoration as a commercial undertaking, by combining the best restoration science with professional forestry industry practice to deliver ecosystem restoration at unprecedented quality and scale. Rainforest Builder’s projects aim to return degraded formerly forested lands to primary levels of biomass, biodiversity and structural complexity rapidly and resiliently, in partnership with a range of stakeholders.\r\n\r\nThe ARR VCS-CCB project is a grouped project that aims to restore approximately 100,000 ha in degraded Forest Reserves in Ghana. The project aims to achieve the sustainable restoration of highly degraded reserve areas through diversified mixed-species plantings that re-establish native flora and fauna, enhance ecological connectivity, and mitigate the adverse effects of deforestation. Central to this endeavour is the goal of ecosystem restoration, achieved with best-practice planting methods to maximise the survival and growth of indigenous species mixes, using species that are carefully selected to re-create natural forest structure. \r\n\r\nThe Climate, Community, and Biodiversity goals of the project are to re-establish and protect natural forest landscapes, recovering threatened biodiversity in a globally important conservation hotspot, sequestering CO2 and improving the provision of ecosystem services including water regulation, nutrient cycling, and climate regulation. The project will provide long-term sustainable employment through reforestation and maintenance activities, promoting economic development and enhancing wellbeing in communities adjacent to project areas.","location":{"latitude":6.144500,"longitude":-2.217193},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2024-09-06","endExclusive":"2024-10-07","endInclusive":"2024-10-06"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"5172"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"West, Central"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Rainforest Builder Ltd."},{"type":"string","value":"London, United Kingdom"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4965"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ARR"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VM0047"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"900 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Earthood Services Limited"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"10/02/2026"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 28/09/2023 - 27/09/2123"}]}]},{"programCode":"CCB","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Rainforest Builder Ltd."},{"type":"string","value":"London, United Kingdom"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Validation approved"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4965"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Afforestation, Reforestation and Revegetation"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"900 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Earthood Services Limited"}]},{"code":"CCB_STANDARD_EDITION_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"CCB Third Edition"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","descri